        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(tool-display): skip heredoc body in splitTopLevelStages",
        "body": "Fixes #102875\n\n## What Problem This Solves\n\nThe stage splitter did not recognize heredoc blocks, causing semicolons and && inside heredoc bodies to be treated as top-level stage separators. This produced phantom failed commands in the tool-status footer.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nWhen an agent uses a heredoc, the ; and && inside the heredoc body were incorrectly split, showing the heredoc content lines as phantom failed commands.\n\n## User Impact\n\nTool-status footers no longer show phantom failed commands from heredoc body content.\n\n## Evidence\n\n- Heredoc body is preserved as one stage (not split on internal separators)\n- Quoted heredoc delimiters work correctly\n- <<-EOF (tab-indented closing) works correctly\n- Normal stage splitting still works for non-heredoc commands\n- Stage separators after heredoc blocks still split correctly",
        "branch": "fix/heredoc-stage-splitter-102875",
